/target
Cargo.lock
*.bits
.DS_Store

# Plan 019 runtime state — the heal self-evolution store + miss queue
# (per-repo runtime data, never committed; see README "Watch mode")
.refine/
# Issue 128 T5: the MINTED ring corpora live under .benchmarks/data and are
# the COMMITTED measurement substrate (per-file BLAKE3 manifests; the
# --fixseq-stats/--horizon-report loader reads them in place). The runtime
# .refine/ rule above stays; this negation re-includes only the committed
# data tree.
!.benchmarks/data/**
CLAUDE.md

# Plan 342 T3.7 default output path (examples/plan342_t37_test_labeled_corpus.rs
# writes ./t37_rows.jsonl when --out is omitted) — a run artifact, not source.
t37_rows.jsonl
.wrangler/

# Plan 199 T3.2: the validator authoring lane's wasm32 build dirs (the
# .wasm ARTIFACTS are committed under assets/validators/; the intermediate
# build trees are not).
validator_src/*/target/
scripts/__pycache__/
.env

# Research 107 — external-source raw clones (distill inputs, never committed:
# a vendored upstream tree would be swept into sibling bulk adds and bloats
# the repo; the distill VERDICT is the record, the clone is disposable).
.raw/

# Issue 044 T7 — the unattended nightly runner writes both of these INTO the
# repo. Untracked files here are not merely noise: sibling agents run bulk
# `git add -A`, and an untracked log/lock is exactly what gets swept into
# someone else's commit.
.benchmarks/ops_nightly.log
.benchmarks/ops_nightly.launchd.log
.benchmarks/healqual_sync.launchd.log
.benchmarks/.ops_nightly.lock/

# session scratch (repro dirs etc.) - sync pass 2026-10-07
.scratch/

# bench raw run artifacts — census/split summaries stay tracked; the heavy
# per-case evidence is regenerable run output (Bench 114 harvest, 1afd5d15)
.benchmarks/114_issue161_pool_widened_harvest/behav/
.benchmarks/114_issue161_pool_widened_harvest/cases.jsonl

# Bench 128 run 8 (2026-11-11, the mitander-reply arc) raw run artifacts —
# the record (a58aa306e) committed the harness + summaries (run8/bench_run8.py,
# run8/rerun-*.out) and the README pins the binaries by sha256 ("run8/bins/,
# NOT committed"); the work-*/rerun-* fixture trees + per-phase logs are
# regenerable by bench_run8.py (same Bench 114 precedent).
.benchmarks/128_mozilla_rustperf_day2/run8/bins/
.benchmarks/128_mozilla_rustperf_day2/run8/bin-*/
.benchmarks/128_mozilla_rustperf_day2/run8/work-*/
.benchmarks/128_mozilla_rustperf_day2/run8/rerun-chain/
.benchmarks/128_mozilla_rustperf_day2/run8/rerun-standalone/
